<p>Palestinians voted on April 25 in municipal elections across the Israeli-occupied West Bank and in Deir al-Balah in central Gaza. The vote marked the first election since the Gaza war and gave some Gazans in the voting area a chance to cast a ballot for the first time in years. Nearly 1.5 million voters were registered in the West Bank and about 70,000 in the Deir al-Balah area, according to the Palestinian Central Elections Commission. The ballot covered local councils, not national institutions, but it still carried political weight beyond routine municipal services. Several reports said the West Bank-based Palestinian Authority saw Deir al-Balah’s inclusion as a symbolic way to reinforce its claim to authority in Gaza, where Hamas ousted it in 2007. At the same time, coverage and analysis stressed that the elections unfolded amid war damage, occupation, and internal Palestinian division, giving voters a rare opening for civic participation but little power over broader national questions.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/5u-LWyaqOFjHdpCoOUyrsAN4L4LsIJjNMjgz-AmpKAB0jbPqBuRneF3zSphRCEZz5hC_OcNk54jaa8svYzCY8kFkIfqj3GVy5bb-MVvmM3jd_jzppBV_Z-2HTYReC80QpgUuaZmLMEK2w-S0AeQqCQlXv6uevjaF9bLyS8M59g' alt='Palestinians take part in local elections in the West Bank and part of Gaza.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Long gap: For Gaza residents in this voting area, the election was described as the first chance to vote since 2005, underscoring how rare this opening was after two decades without a ballot there.</li><li>Local issues: In Deir al-Balah, candidates focused on practical municipal needs such as water and sanitation, showing how strongly daily services shaped the campaign even as larger political questions remained unresolved.</li><li>Trust test: Several outlets said the vote could test public confidence in Palestinian institutions after the war, especially in areas dealing with damaged infrastructure and political fragmentation.</li><li>Limited scope: Al Jazeera’s analysis argued that the ballot offered participation without sovereignty, because local councils operate within constraints imposed by occupation and the absence of full Palestinian self-rule.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Palestinian Authority: The West Bank-based Palestinian Authority hopes that including Deir al-Balah in the vote will symbolically reinforce its claim to govern Gaza as well as the West Bank. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/palestinian-local-elections-on-april-25-gazans-vote-for-the-first-time-in-years/article70904464.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Hamas: Hamas ousted the Palestinian Authority from Gaza in 2007, shaping the political backdrop for a vote held only in part of the territory rather than across all of Gaza. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/palestinian-local-elections-on-april-25-gazans-vote-for-the-first-time-in-years/article70904464.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera analysis: The elections represent civic participation with sharply limited power, arguing that occupation defines what local voting can and cannot change in Palestinian political life. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/opinions/2026/4/25/elections-without-sovereignty-what-palestines-local-vote-really-represent'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Voters and local communities: Residents in Deir al-Balah had a rare chance to choose representatives who could address immediate municipal concerns such as water and sanitation while also expressing hopes for wider Palestinian unity. (<a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Middle-East/2026/0424/gaza-elections-hamas-palestinian-unity-democracy'>The Christian Science Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/palestinian-local-elections-on-april-25-gazans-vote-for-the-first-time-in-years/article70904464.ece'>Palestinian local elections give some Gazans a chance to vote for the first time in years</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/opinions/2026/4/25/elections-without-sovereignty-what-palestines-local-vote-really-represent'>Elections without sovereignty: What Palestine’s local vote really represent</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/palestinians-vote-in-municipal-elections-in-gaza-west-bank/a-76930149'>Palestinians vote in municipal elections in Gaza, West Bank</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Middle-East/2026/0424/gaza-elections-hamas-palestinian-unity-democracy'>In Gaza, rare elections put hope, and talk of Palestinian unity, on the ballot</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/palestinians-to-vote-in-1st-elections-in-20-years-11406300#publisher=newsstand'>Palestinians To Vote In 1st Elections In 20 Years</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/local-elections-west-bank-part-gaza-test-public-132371182'>Local elections in the West Bank and part of Gaza could test public trust</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.youtube.com/watch'>Palestinian&#x27;s vote in Gaza, West Bank elections under shadow of Hamas • FRANCE 24 English</a> - youtube.com</li></ul>